          "distinct": false,
          "id": "bad95337089a7c16731598798afd4dfa6720f9a4",
          "message": "bench(consolidate): dominance gap-table v2 — merge canonical wave-1 + D3 re-measure + materialization (sq-hmd7l.27) [OPUS-4.8] (#1829)\n\nConsolidates every landed research/gap-<axis>-2026-07.md row plus the newly\ncommitted inputs into research/perf-dominance-gap-2026-07.md §9 under the fixed\nverdict vocabulary (CLEARLY-AHEAD / AHEAD-BUT-NOT-OOM / PARITY / BEHIND /\nNOT-MEASURED / NOT-COMPARABLE). No new measurements — committed evidence only.\n\nFolded in:\n- canonical wave-1 (fts/geo/hdt/update/parse, sq-hmd7l.26 #1809)\n- canonical SP2Bench D3 re-measure (sq-7d3dj.30.6 #1827): 10/14 vs same-box\n  QLever, correct+complete on all 14; §3 pre-fix per-query BEHIND rows now cite\n  their superseding bead\n- materialization D6 (#1799 + VLog/Nemo encodings #1823; canonical univ>=100\n  in flight sq-hmd7l.32 -> NOT-MEASURED, cited)\n\nEvery BEHIND/PARITY table row carries a filed P1/P2 profiling-first fix bead;\nevery NOT-MEASURED cites its blocking bead; every cell cites its envelope\nfilename or gap record. RDFox published columns per-core-normalized. Failed/\nabsent competitors (fuseki-absent D13, jena 0-hits D15c, hdt-cpp fixture-scale\nD16) are re-run actions / NOT-MEASURED / NOT-COMPARABLE, never wins.\n\nNew fix beads filed (P1, profiling-first): sq-p7kk5 (SPARQL-UPDATE p99 BEHIND\noxigraph ~6.6x), sq-wrn61 (single-thread Turtle parse BEHIND serd ~2.0x),\nsq-7jt80 (geof:sfWithin ~600x slower than within* — full-scan, self-slow gap).\nReused existing: sq-7d3dj.30.20/.21/.22, sq-jnb1e, sq-hmd7l.32, sq-tvzyi,\nsq-a8anf, sq-do5fx, sq-l7diu.\n\nmarkdownlint (cli2@0.18.1) + typos clean; acceptance grep confirms every\nBEHIND/PARITY table row contains an sq- bead id.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jesse@jeswr.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
